:: D01_Panic [nobr]
<<HUD>>

<<ImagePlaceholder "Huddled on the bathroom floor, knees to chest, crying" "portrait" "assets/characters/mc-female-phase1/bathroom-floor-panic.png">>

<div class="prose-block">

<p>I sit down on the bathroom floor, cold tile against legs that are smooth and wrong and somehow still mine.</p>

<p>I pull my knees to my chest and they come in closer than they should. My hips flex at a different angle now, wider, more accommodating. Even sitting feels different. Even the way my body folds up is different.</p>

<p>My breathing goes fast and shallow. The panic response feels different in this body, my heart pounds higher up in my chest, the adrenaline hits differently, there&apos;s a tightness in my throat that makes the air feel thin. I&apos;m hyperventilating. I know I&apos;m hyperventilating. I can&apos;t make it stop.</p>

<p>Tears come without me deciding anything, an involuntary flood like a faucet someone turned on without asking my permission. I haven&apos;t cried in three years. Not when my dad forgot my birthday. Not when my grandmother&apos;s house got sold. Not when the loan letters started piling up. Three years of drought, and now tears are streaming down my face like my body decided to process every unprocessed emotion at once.</p>

<p>&quot;What the fuck. What the fuck, what the fuck...&quot;</p>

<p>My voice. My actual voice. It isn&apos;t mine anymore. The words are the same but the register is wrong, higher, softer, a mid-alto where there used to be a tired tenor. It cracks when I shout, but it cracks upward now, not downward. I hear myself speak and the person speaking is a woman.</p>

<p>I grab my phone off the floor, hands shaking. The phone feels too big now, my palm is smaller, my grip is different. I fumble the passcode twice before it lets me in.</p>

<p>I dial NovaCure.</p>

<p>It goes to voicemail. &quot;NovaCure Laboratories is currently closed. Our business hours are 9 AM to...&quot;</p>

<p>I hang up and dial again. Same message. I check the time, 7:48 AM. They don&apos;t open for another hour.</p>

<p>I sit on the bathroom floor in my dead grandmother&apos;s hoodie, swimming on me now, in boxers that won&apos;t stay up on hips six inches wider than they were eight hours ago. I sit there and I cry and I wait.</p>

<p>At 9:15 I try again. A different voice than last night&apos;s receptionist. I try to explain, and the words come out in a torrent of panic and broken sentences.</p>

<<Dialogue "You" "😰" "I need to speak to Dr. Amelia. Now. Something happened. Something... I'm... my body..." "you">>

<<Dialogue "NovaCure Intake" "☎️" "Sir, can you describe..." "">>

<<Dialogue "You" "😰" "I WOKE UP AS A WOMAN." "you">>

<p>A long pause follows, so long I check to see if the call dropped.</p>

<<Dialogue "NovaCure Intake" "☎️" "...2 PM, Mr. Cole. I'm sorry, can you come in at 2 PM? We'll have Dr. Amelia available." "">>

<<Dialogue "You" "😰" "I'll be there." "you">>

<p>I hang up. Five hours. I have to exist in this body for five more hours before anyone can even look at me and tell me what happened, then fix it, fix me, change me back.</p>

<p>I stand up and catch my reflection in the mirror again. The woman on the bathroom floor, tear streaked, hair a total mess, drowning in a man&apos;s hoodie, scared out of her mind.</p>

<p>She looks like me. She looks like my grandmother. She looks like nobody I&apos;ve ever met in my life.</p>

<p>I look away first.</p>

</div>

<div class="choice-block">
	<<link '<span>Try to hold it together</span>' "Home">>
		<<set $mustReturnToNovaCure to true>>
		<<run window.rbAddJournalEntry("Something Happened", "I woke up transformed. NovaCure can see me at 2 PM. I don't know how I'm supposed to exist until then.")>>
	<</link>>
</div>
